 ahead of you and then  swimming again so let me reset this what  you want to be doing is inking diving  down popping up and then inking again  and then popping down or diving down  popping up and you want to repeat this  process because this will get you from  point A to point B as quickly as  possible you can see I do a little jump  in there and that's mostly because  you know just it's a personal thing it  kind of helps with my rhythm you know  the game is very rhythmic you know not  only the music but like just the flow of  the matches and the characters so you  want to be so what I like doing is just  jumping up shooting it diving down  jumping up shooting I'm not sure exactly  if it gives you more distance your shot  I still have to look at the numbers but  um you know either way I'm going to be  diving down hugging back up and then  shooting you you don't need to worry too  much about these small gaps in the ink  that I have so like between right here  for example you can swim right through  that and it won't slow you down too much  but if there are like bigger gaps like  this you might have a little bit of  problem going through it you can see you  like that  you can see the squid actually right  there but for the most part just smaller  gaps don't worry too much about it is  you can just you know swim straight  through it alright so for topic two  we're gonna be talking about engaging  and avoiding so you know movement is not  only about getting to one place as fast  as possible that is important but what  might be even more important at times is  the ability to get away from everyone  you know if you come across an inkling  with a special on deck you can see  they're blowing air right here if they  have that or that back up or if they or  if you're just in their own territory  and the non lager ink is on the ground  you want to be able to get away as fast  as possible one of the things that I  like doing is looking for a higher  ground so for example if you're being  chased right here and you see a little  ledge like this you can ink the sides  and swim up and then you have like a  good job though good shot at them from a  bucket above here another thing that you  can do is use the the bonds or your sub  weapons so for example the Aero spray  here has the suction bomb so what I like  doing while I'm being chased by someone  is swimming laying a bomb down and then  continuing to swim and that way they  they won't be able to follow me or they  won't be able to be right on my tail you  know they're gonna have to watch out for  the bomb so they don't get spotted  and then one of the other things I want  to mention is that the the method for  inking you know diving down to the ink  jumping up inking diving down again that  works just as well for when you're  trying to get away probably even more so  probably even more important to do that  when you're getting away because you got  to be fast if you're swimming through  other people's ink you want to make sure  you have a path and so you want to be  jump up ink dive down as soon as  possible you know you want you want to  try to get away and try to find your  teammates group up with them and then  gang up on the other guy that was  shooting at you and the third topic  we're going to be talking about here is  vertical movement and now I touched on  this just a little bit earlier about you  know inking a wall and then climbing up  to get a get a better shot at someone  from from above but just overall  vertical movement in this game is very  very important and you want to make sure  to utilize it as as often as possible so  what you can do is you can ink a wall  and then swim up it just like that to  get to higher grounds but what what you  always want to be doing when you when  you're swimming up is make sure you're  mashing be mashing the jump button to  make sure you swim faster I see this a  lot and some people just kind of might  okay it will kind of slip your mind  sometimes when you're when you're  swimming because you know you don't  press B except to jump out like that so  it kind of makes sense suggesting you'll  swim up at the same rate but you can see  the difference here in the speed this is  me swimming without pressing form  without mashing B looks like that and  this is with me mashing you know you can  hear that that little squishy sound you  know of your of yourself mashing B and  you'll swim much faster going uphill or  going up walls it's one of my favorite  things to do another thing I really like  doing is utilizing the walls for sneak  attacks if you for example are being  chased by someone and you go around the  wall and you this wall is empty or it  has your ink color what you can do is go  like this go around the corner and then  immediately jump onto  wall and you can kind of a kind of fill  with the with the up direction kind of  just hold it up for a second and then  let go kind of stay in one place and  that way if they come around the corner  they're going to be expecting you to be  here at some point but if you go around  they're not gonna be able to see this  and jump onto the wall you can wait for  them to come around we just completely  confuse as to where you went pop out and  then splat them it's the the game is  very much built around sneak attacks  you know just hiding in ink and waiting  and so doing that on the walls is  probably one of the most uh clever  things you can do alright so thanks for  watching I hope you guys learned a thing  or two about movement in the game you  know it's gonna take a little bit of  practice but once you get once you get  going and once you know how to move  you're gonna have a really great time in  in splatoon too now if you guys enjoyed  this video leave a like or even  subscribe to the channel if you want to  catch our second lesson in which I'll be  talking about the weapons in the game  but for now I'll leave you with a little  bit of gameplay from one of my matches  so you can study that and be ready for  the next lesson all right I'll see you  guys then  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]
 

